 "仕損じ": "فَشَل, قُصُور (State or condition of not meeting a desirable or intended objective, opposite of) / فَشَل (An object, person or endeavour in a state of failure, has failed at something or) / عُطْل (Termination of the ability of an item to perform its required function; breakdow)  [failure]",
 "仕損じる": "أَخْفَقَ, فَشِلَ (To be unsuccessful.) / رَسَبَ (To receive one or more non-passing grades in academic pursuits.)  [to fail]\nمثال: 急いては事を仕損じるよ。もう少々慎重に。\n→ Be more careful. Rushing through things is going to ruin your work.",
