 "以上": "[not less than ... ; ... and over]\nمثال: ６歳以上の子供は学校に通わなければならない。\n→ Children of six and above should attend school. / أَبْعَد (Further away than.) / أَقْصَى (On the far side of.) / بَعْد (Later than; after.) / فَوْق (Greater than; so as to exceed or surpass.) / فَوْقَ (In addition to; supplementing.)  [beyond (e.g. one's expectations)]\nمثال: これ以上の値引きは、私どもを赤字に追いやるでしょう。\n→ A further reduction would make us go into the red. / أَعْلَى (Physically over; on top of; worn on top of, said of clothing.) / فَوقَ (In or to a higher place; higher than; on or over the upper surface.) / شَمَالِيّ (Farther north than.) / أَعْلَى (Higher than; superior to in any respect; surpassing; higher in measure, degree, ) / على (In preference to.)  [the above]\nمثال: 以上のように、実にシンプルな誰でも出来るノウハウで十分な利益と顧客は確保できるのです！\n→ As shown above, it is possible to obtain ample profit and customers with truly simple know-how that anyone can do! / [since ... ; seeing that ...]\nafter a verb\nمثال: 公僕も人間であること、また、人間である以上過ちを犯す可能性があることを、彼は認識している。\n→ He realizes that public officials are human, and that as human beings they are capable of misjudgement.",
 "以下": "[not exceeding ... ; not more than ...]\nمثال: １６歳以下の子供は劇場には入場できません。\n→ Children of age sixteen and under will not be admitted to the theatre. / تَحْتَ (Lower in spatial position than.) / جَنُوبِيّ (South of.)  [below (a standard, level, etc.)]\nمثال: 君の要約は平均以下だね。\n→ Your summary is not up to par. / تَالٍ, التَّالِي (Coming next, either in sequence or in time.) / بَعْد (After, subsequent to.)  [the following]\nمثال: 以下の説明は多くの異なる理論を比較的対照することによって得られたものである。\n→ The explanation below was achieved by comparing and contrasting a variety of different theories. / [including ... ; ... and other (employees, officials, etc.)]\nused to refer to all members of a group, starting with the head or principal figure",
 "以下の通り": "كَمَا يَلِي (In the manner described hereafter.)  [as follows]",
 "以内": "دَاخِل (In the inner part, spatially; physically inside.) / في غضون (In the scope or range of.) / فِي خِلَال (Before the specified duration ends.)  [within]\nمثال: １週間以内に電話します。\n→ I'll call you within a week.",
