 "何ごとも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [everything]\nمثال: トムは何事も楽しんでやるんだ。\n→ Tom enjoys himself at everything he does. / لَا شَيْء (Not any thing; no thing.)  [nothing]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: この古い村では何事も起こらない。\n→ Nothing ever happens in this old village.",
 "何さま": "أَحَد (One or some person of unspecified or indefinite identity.)  [a someone]\noften used sarcastically\nمثال: 自分を何様だと思っているのだ、人をそんな風に見て。\n→ Who do you think you are, to look at me like this? / مطلقا, على الإطلاق (In an absolute or unconditional manner; utterly, positively, wholly.)  [absolutely]",
 "何しろ": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]\nمثال: 何しろ小さい店なので、彼は会計係から倉庫係まで多くの仕事を一手にこなさなければならない。\n→ Because the store is so small, he has to wear many different hats, from accountant to stock boy. / لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "何じゃ": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nemphatic",
 "何するものぞ": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "何せ": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]\nمثال: 我々はボロ勝ちした。何せ相手の選手ときたら弱いのなんの。\n→ We won hands down, because the other players were weak.",
 "何ぞ": "شَيْء (An uncertain or unspecified thing; one thing.)  [something] / يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what] / لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]",
 "何ぞや": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what] / لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]",
 "何たって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "何たる": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what (e.g. \"what rudeness\")]\nexpression of surprise, anger / [what (something) is like]\nusu. as 〜の何たるか\nمثال: 彼女はもう１０年もフランス語を勉強しているのだから、フランス語の何たるかはよくわかっているはずだ。\n→ She has been studying French for ten years, so she ought to realize what French is.",
 "何だ": "وَا, يَا or يَاه (Expression of surprise.) / آه (Expression of understanding, affirmation, recognition, or realization.) / يَا, أَيْ (An invocation or address (similar to the vocative in languages with noun declens)  [oh]\nمثال: 「そっか。暇なら掃除しといて」「なんだそれ。兄貴をアゴで使うなよ」\n→ \"Oh? If you're free get the cleaning done.\" \"What's up with that? Don't order your brother around!\" / لَعَنَ (To condemn.) / لَعَنَ (To curse; put a curse upon.) / اللَّعْنَة (Used to express anger, irritation, disappointment, annoyance, contempt or surpri)  [damn]",
 "何だか": "صَغِير, صغير (Small, not large, limited) / قَلِيلاً, قَلِيل (Not much.) / قَلِيل (Not much, only a little: only a small amount (of).)  [(a) little]\nمثال: なんだかすごく辛いの。\n→ Somehow it's been a rough day.",
 "何だって": "[what?! ; what did you say?!] / [why? ; what for?]\nمثال: 何だって私の本がこんなところにあるんだろう。\n→ What's my book doing here? / أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]\nمثال: そんな席からコンサートが聴けたら、人は、何だってするさ。\n→ People would sell their souls to hear the concert from those seats.",
 "何ちゅう": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (beautiful, etc.)] / [nothing worth mentioning ; nothing special] / [of what name]",
 "何つったって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "何てこった": "مَاذَا بِحَقّ اَلسَّمَاء (An intensive form of what.)  [what the hell]",
 "何てことない": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]",
 "何てことのない": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]",
 "何てったって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "何であれ": "أَيّ, أَيَّمَا (Regardless of the ... that; for any ... that.) / مَهْمَا مَا (What ever; emphasised form of 'what', used to ask which thing, event, circumstan) / طُز (A holophrastic expression used to dismiss something that the speaker doesn't car)  [whatever]\nمثال: なんであれ物事の本体を捕らえる事が肝心だ。\n→ No matter what the problem is, it's essential to get at the heart of the matter.",
 "何でかと言うと": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "何でも": "أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nمثال: この犬は何でもほとんど食べます。\n→ This dog eats almost anything. / [I am told ; I hear]\nat start of sentence",
 "何でもかでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [(anything and) everything] / [by all means ; at any cost]",
 "何でもかんでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [(anything and) everything]\nمثال: 聞いた事をなんでもかんでも信じてはいけない。\n→ Don't believe everything you hear. / [by all means ; at any cost]",
 "何でもない": "سَهْل (Requiring little skill or effort.)  [easy]\nمثال: 何でもないことに大騒ぎするのはやめなさい。\n→ Stop making a fuss over nothing. / عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]\nin the form of 〜でもなんでもない",
 "何でも彼でも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [(anything and) everything] / [by all means ; at any cost]",
 "何でも無い": "سَهْل (Requiring little skill or effort.)  [easy]\nمثال: 何でもないことに大騒ぎするのはやめなさい。\n→ Stop making a fuss over nothing. / عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]\nin the form of 〜でもなんでもない",
 "何と": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: 英語でこの昆虫を何といいますか。\n→ What do you call this insect in English? / [what (a) ...! ; how ...!]\nindicates surprise, admiration, etc.\nمثال: なんと素晴らしい発明だろう。\n→ What a wonderful invention! / صدق أو لا تصدق (This may be surprising, but it's true.)  [believe it or not] / عَجَبًا (An indication of excitement, surprise, astonishment, or pleasure.) / سُبْحَانَ الله (An expression of amazement, awe, or admiration.)  [wow]",
 "何という": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (beautiful, tasty, etc.)]\nمثال: なんというばかげた考えだ。\n→ What an absurd idea! / [nothing worth mentioning ; nothing special]\nwith neg. verb, esp. as ～こともない / [of what name]",
 "何とか": "شَيْء (An uncertain or unspecified thing; one thing.)  [something] / بِطَرِيقَةٍ أَو بِأُخرَى (By any means possible.)  [one way or another]\nمثال: なんとかその機械を動かした。\n→ He managed to run the machine.",
 "何とかして": "بِطَرِيقَةٍ أَو بِأُخرَى (By any means possible.)  [one way or another]",
 "何としてでも": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: 私は何としてでも自分の目的を成し遂げます。\n→ I will accomplish my purpose at any cost.",
 "何としても": "بِأَيِّ ثَمَنٍ (As an absolute imperative; sparing no effort or expense)  [at all costs]\nمثال: 医者と看護婦はなんとしても生命を守らなければならない。\n→ Doctors and nurses must preserve life at all costs.",
 "何とぞ": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: 浅学非才の私ではありますが、何とぞ皆様のお力を賜りたく、ここにお願い申し上げる次第です。\n→ I may not have much to offer in the way of learning or ability, but I want to do whatever I can for us all and humbly ask for your favor. / [by all means ; without fail]",
 "何とでも": "أَيّ, أَيَّمَا (Regardless of the ... that; for any ... that.) / مَهْمَا مَا (What ever; emphasised form of 'what', used to ask which thing, event, circumstan) / طُز (A holophrastic expression used to dismiss something that the speaker doesn't car)  [whatever]",
 "何となれば": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "何とも": "حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nمثال: 何とも言いようがないなあ。\n→ I just don't know what to say. / أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [(not) anything]\nwith neg. verb",
 "何ともない": "أَمِين, سَالِم (Not in danger; out of harm's reach.) / خَزْنَة حَدِيدِيَّة, خَزْنَة (A box, usually made of metal, in which valuables can be locked for safekeeping.)  [safe (and sound)]",
 "何ともはや": "حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]\nemphatic",
 "何とも無い": "أَمِين, سَالِم (Not in danger; out of harm's reach.) / خَزْنَة حَدِيدِيَّة, خَزْنَة (A box, usually made of metal, in which valuables can be locked for safekeeping.)  [safe (and sound)]",
 "何と言う": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how (beautiful, tasty, etc.)]\nمثال: なんというばかげた考えだ。\n→ What an absurd idea! / [nothing worth mentioning ; nothing special]\nwith neg. verb, esp. as ～こともない / [of what name]",
 "何と言うか": "حَبَّ (to enjoy) / أَحَبَّ (to enjoy) / اِسْتَمْطَعَ (to enjoy) / أَعْجَبَ (to enjoy) / مِثْل (Similar.) / مِثْل, شِبْه (Someone similar to a given person, or something similar to a given object; a com) / مِثْل, كَـ (Similar to, reminiscent of.) / مِثْل, كَـ (Such as; including.)  [like]",
 "何と言ったって": "مَهْمَا (Regardless of, in spite of, whatever.)  [no matter what]",
 "何なら": "[if you like ; if you prefer]\nمثال: 何ならジョージの職場に電話をして、すぐ帰宅してお前を手伝うようにと伝えようかい。\n→ In fact, I'll even call George at the office and tell him he ought to come home and help out. / [if ... doesn't suit you ; if you don't like ...]\nas ...が何なら / عِلَاوَة عَلَى ذٰلِكَ, أَضِف إِلَى ذٰلِك (In addition; besides; further; what's more (i.e. to denote additional informatio)  [furthermore] / آنَذَاكَ, حِينَئِذٍ (At that time.) / ثُمَّ (Soon afterward.) / ثُمَّ (Next in order of place.) / إِذًا, إِذَنْ (In that case.)  [then]",
 "何なり": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]\nمثال: 何なりと言って下さい。\n→ Just tell me what you'd like me to do.",
 "何なりと": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]",
 "何なりとも": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything]",
 "何にしろ": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "何にせよ": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "何にでも": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [everything]\nمثال: 要するに彼は何にでも飽きるのだ。\n→ In a word, he tires of everything.",
 "何にも": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [(not) anything]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: このロボット何でも私の言うことを聞くんだ。疲れて、何にもしたくない時は、助かるね。なんて、ありえない話だよね。\n→ This robot does whatever I say. That's a big help when I'm too tired to do anything. Not too likely, huh?",
 "何にもならない": "عَقِيم (Unproductive, useless.)  [fruitless]\nمثال: 彼の過去の成功は何にもならない。\n→ His past successes count for nothing.",
 "何の": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: 何の目的で彼はここに来たのか。\n→ For what purpose did he come here? / أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nwith. neg. sentence\nمثال: その噂はなんの根拠もなかった。\n→ The rumor was without foundation. / [adds emphasis to the preceding word]\nas ...のなんの\nمثال: 彼女、美しいのなんのって・・・！\n→ She is beautiful and how! / لَا (Not any.) / نَعَم (Used to show agreement with a negative question.) / لَا, لَاءَان (A negating expression; an answer that shows disagreement, denial, refusal, or di) / لَا (A vote not in favor, or opposing a proposition.)  [no]\nused to dismiss someone's concerns, words, etc.",
 "何のこった": "مَاذَا بِحَقّ اَلسَّمَاء (An intensive form of what.)  [what the hell]",
 "何のこと": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what] / [something out of the ordinary ; something unusual] / [what the heck ; holy cow!]",
 "何のことはない": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "何のことは無い": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "何の事": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what] / [something out of the ordinary ; something unusual] / [what the heck ; holy cow!]",
 "何の事はない": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "何の事は無い": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "何の変哲もない": "بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain]",
 "何の変哲も無い": "بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain]",
 "何の役にも立たない": "عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]\nمثال: 杖は彼に何の役にも立たなかった。\n→ The stick didn't help him any.",
 "何の様に": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]\nمثال: あなたはどのようにしてその問題を解いたのですか。\n→ How did you solve the problem?",
 "何の気なしに": "عَنْ غَفْلَةٍ (Without meaning to, in an unintentional manner, not intentionally.)  [unintentionally]\nمثال: なんの気なしに言っただけで、別に悪気があってのことではありません。\n→ I just said so without thinking much about it. I didn't mean anything serious.",
 "何はさておき": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]",
 "何はともあれ": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]\nمثال: 何はともあれ、大事にいたらなかったのは、不幸中の幸いであった。\n→ At any rate, that it had ended without serious incident was a small mercy.",
 "何ひとつ": "وَاحِد, وَاحِدَة (The number represented by the Arabic numeral 1; the numerical value equal to tha) / اَلْمَرْء (Any person (applying to people in general).)  [(not) one]\nusu. in neg. phrases\nمثال: 彼は子供たちに何一つだめだと言わない。\n→ He denies nothing to his children.",
 "何びと": "مَنْ (Any person or persons that.)  [whoever]\nمثال: 何びとも奴隷の状態に留め置かれてはならない。\n→ No one shall be held in slavery.",
 "何ぶん": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some] / أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please] / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]\nمثال: なにぶんこんな辺ぴな村に住んでいるので、めったに客は来ない。\n→ Living as I do in a remote village, I seldom have visitors.",
 "何ほど": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much]",
 "何ぼ": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much]\nesp. used in Kansai / بِأَيَّةِ طَرِيقَة, عَلَى كُلِّ حَال (In any way that one likes or chooses; in a haphazard or spontaneous way.)  [however (much)]\nas なんぼ...〜ても, なんぼ...〜でも, etc. / [what matters is ... ; it all comes down to ...]\nas 〜てなんぼ",
 "何ぼう": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much] / بِأَيَّةِ طَرِيقَة, عَلَى كُلِّ حَال (In any way that one likes or chooses; in a haphazard or spontaneous way.)  [however (much)]\nas なんぼう...〜とも, etc.",
 "何も": "أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [(not) anything]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: 過ちのない者は何も作り出せない。\n→ He who makes no mistakes makes nothing. / [and everything else ; and all]\nas ...も何も\nمثال: 車も何もなく、生活保護で生きてます。\n→ I'm living on welfare, without a car or anything. / أبداً (Indicating degree, quantity or frequency greater than zero: to the slightest deg)  [(not) at all]\nas ...なくてもいい, ...ことはない, etc.",
 "何もの": "مَن, مين (What person or people; which person or people; asks for the identity of someone;)  [who]\nمثال: そこで、今の人達が何者なのか説明しておきたいと思います。\n→ So I want to explain who these people are.",
 "何ものか": "أَحَد (One or some person of unspecified or indefinite identity.)  [someone]\nمثال: 何者かが彼女を浴槽で溺死させた。\n→ Somebody had drowned her in the bathtub.",
 "何やつ": "مَن, مين (What person or people; which person or people; asks for the identity of someone;)  [who]",
 "何やら": "شَيْء (An uncertain or unspecified thing; one thing.)  [something]\nمثال: 私はなにやら彼に話さなければならないことがある。\n→ I have something or other to tell him. / [for some reason]\nمثال: なにやら唸りながら、ほとばしるパッションをキャンバスにぶつけている！\n→ Groaning strangely she is hurling her overflowing passion onto the canvas!",
 "何ゆえ": "لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]",
 "何より": "[above anything else ; above all]\nمثال: 何より大事なことは、自分の頭で考えることだ。\n→ The most important thing is thinking for oneself. / أَفْضَل (superlative form of good: most good.)  [best]\nمثال: 私は自分が健康で何よりだと思っている。\n→ I count myself lucky in having good health.",
 "何よりもまず": "بَادِئَ ذِي بَدْءٍ (Primarily; most importantly.)  [first and foremost]\nمثال: 何よりもまず、老人に親切にするように努めなさい。\n→ Above all, try to be kind to the old.",
 "何よりも先ず": "بَادِئَ ذِي بَدْءٍ (Primarily; most importantly.)  [first and foremost]\nمثال: 何よりもまず、老人に親切にするように努めなさい。\n→ Above all, try to be kind to the old.",
 "何ら": "أبداً (Indicating degree, quantity or frequency greater than zero: to the slightest deg)  [(not) at all]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: 彼はその不正事件に何ら関わりがなかった。\n→ He had no part in the scandal. / [what kind of]",
 "何らか": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]\nمثال: これを解く何らかの方法があるはずだ。\n→ There must be some way to solve this.",
 "何れ": "أَيّ (What, of those mentioned or implied.) / مَما (Designates the one(s) previously mentioned.) / أَيّ (What one or ones (of those mentioned or implied).) / اَلَّذِي (In a non-restrictive relative clause, referring to something previously mentione)  [which]\nمثال: 作家としての彼女は伝統的なカテゴリーのいずれにも当てはまらない。\n→ As a writer, she does not fit into any of the traditional categories. / كُلّ, جَمِيع (Every individual or anything of the given class, with no exceptions (the noun or) / كُلّ, جَمِيع (Wholly; entirely; completely; totally.) / جَمِيع (Everything that one is capable of.)  [all]\nas いずれも or いずれの...も / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway] / عَاجِلاً أَم آجِلاً, عَاجِلاً أَو آجِلاً (Eventually, at some undetermined time in the not-too-distant future.)  [sooner or later]\nمثال: いずれどこかに落ち着いて身を固めるつもりだが、まだまだだ。\n→ Eventually I'd like to settle down and have a family, but not yet.",
 "何れか": "وَاحِد, وَاحِدَة (The number represented by the Arabic numeral 1; the numerical value equal to tha) / اَلْمَرْء (Any person (applying to people in general).)  [one (of)]\nمثال: 選ぶべき道はただ１つ成功か死かのいずれか。\n→ The only alternatives are success and death.",
 "何れにしても": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]\nمثال: チャンスというものはいずれにしても、まれにしかない。\n→ Chances come rarely in any case.",
 "何れにしろ": "عَلَى أَيِّ حَالٍ (Whatever be the case.)  [in any case]\nمثال: いずれにしろ、明日は列車に乗りなさい。\n→ In any case, catch the train tomorrow.",
 "何れにせよ": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]\nمثال: いずれにせよ、その隔たりは現実のものであり、実際に役に立つものではあるのだが、同時にそれは誤解を招くおそれのあるものでもある。\n→ In either case, the division is real and useful; but it can also be misleading.",
 "何れにも": "لَا أَحَد (Not any of a given number or group.)  [none]\nwith verb in the negative\nمثال: このコンピューターは品質ではどれにも劣らない。\n→ This computer is second to none in quality.",
 "何れも": "أَيّ (One at all; at least one; at least one kind of; some; a positive quantity of.) / أَيّ (A/an, each or some, no matter its/their identity or nature.) / أَيّ, كُلّ (Any thing(s) or person(s).)  [any]\nمثال: その本はどれも読んでない。\n→ I have not read all the books.",
 "何れも此れも": "كُلّ, جَمِيع (Every individual or anything of the given class, with no exceptions (the noun or) / كُلّ, جَمِيع (Wholly; entirely; completely; totally.) / جَمِيع (Everything that one is capable of.)  [all]\nمثال: あの喜劇役者のジョークときたら、どれもこれも古くて、以前に聞いたことのあるものばかりだ。\n→ That comic's jokes are all old hat and we've heard them before.",
 "何を": "[what?] / لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]",
 "何ヵ月も": "شَهْر (A period into which a year is divided, historically based on the phases of the m)  [(for) months]",
 "何ヶ月も": "شَهْر (A period into which a year is divided, historically based on the phases of the m)  [(for) months]",
 "何一つ": "وَاحِد, وَاحِدَة (The number represented by the Arabic numeral 1; the numerical value equal to tha) / اَلْمَرْء (Any person (applying to people in general).)  [(not) one]\nusu. in neg. phrases\nمثال: 彼は子供たちに何一つだめだと言わない。\n→ He denies nothing to his children.",
 "何事": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nمثال: 何事が起こったのか誰もが知りたがっていた。\n→ Everybody was anxious to know what had happened. / كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [everything]\nمثال: 私の友人は１年に３つも職を変えた。何事にも長続きはしないのだ。\n→ My friend has had three jobs in a year; he never sticks to anything for long. / [what (on earth)? ; what's the meaning of this ...?]\nused to rebuke someone\nمثال: 彼の信念は何事にも揺るがなかった。\n→ Nothing could sway his conviction.",
 "何事か": "شَيْء (An uncertain or unspecified thing; one thing.)  [something (or other)]\nمثال: 何事かが今にも起こりそうなけはいを感じていた。\n→ He felt that something was about to happen.",
 "何事も": "كُلّ شَيْء (All the things under discussion.)  [everything]\nمثال: トムは何事も楽しんでやるんだ。\n→ Tom enjoys himself at everything he does. / لَا شَيْء (Not any thing; no thing.)  [nothing]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: この古い村では何事も起こらない。\n→ Nothing ever happens in this old village.",
 "何人": "مَنْ (Any person or persons that.)  [whoever]\nمثال: 何びとも奴隷の状態に留め置かれてはならない。\n→ No one shall be held in slavery.",
 "何人も": "مَن, مين (What person or people; which person or people; asks for the identity of someone;)  [(no matter) who]\nمثال: 何人も空の胃の腑では愛国者たり得ない。\n→ No man can be a patriot on an empty stomach. / [nobody]\nwith neg. verb",
 "何何": "يَا لَ (Emphasises that something is noteworthy or remarkable in quality or degree, in e) / مَا (That which; those that; the thing(s) that.) / مَاذَا, مَا (Anything that; all that; whatever.)  [what]\nused when asking about or referring to multiple unspecified things / فُلَان, فُلَانَة (A placeholder name for a person or thing, used when a name is not known; a gener)  [so-and-so]\nused when listing things that are unknown or do not need to be specified / اِنْتَظَرَ (To delay movement or action until some event or time; to remain neglected or in )  [wait]\nused when asking for confirmation upon hearing something surprising / [well, well ; let's see]\nused when about to read a letter or document",
 "何兆": "بِلْيُون (a million million, 1012 — see also billion) / تِرِيلِيُون (a million million, 1012 — see also billion) / تِرِيلِْيُون (a million million million, 1018 — see also quintillion)  [(many) trillions]",
 "何処": "أَيْن, فين (In, at or to what place.) / حَيْثُ (The place in, at or to which.) / أَيْن (The place in which something happens.)  [where]\nمثال: あなたはどこでテレビを見ますか。\n→ Where do you watch television? / كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much (long, far)]",
 "何処いら": "أَيْن, فين (In, at or to what place.) / حَيْثُ (The place in, at or to which.) / أَيْن (The place in which something happens.)  [where]",
 "何処から何処まで": "جَمِيع أَنْحَاء, كُلّ (Everywhere; covering completely.)  [all over (the place)]",
 "何処にでもある": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]",
 "何処にでもいる": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]\nمثال: 僕にはどこにでもいるおっさんとしか見えないけどなあ。\n→ To me he's no different from a million other dull middle aged men.",
 "何処にも": "فِي لَا مَكَان (In no place.)  [nowhere]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: 指輪はどこにも見つからなかった。\n→ The ring was not to be found anywhere. / فِي كُلِّ مَكَانٍ (In or to all locations under discussion.)  [everywhere]\nمثال: ここでも、このアプローチがマシュー・アーノルドの「どこにも連結がある」という考えに由来していることを見て取ることができる。\n→ Again, we can see this approach as deriving from Matthew Arnold's idea that everywhere there is connection.",
 "何処にも彼処にも": "جَمِيع أَنْحَاء, كُلّ (Everywhere; covering completely.)  [all over]\nمثال: そして、つい先日迄、暗い感じだったのに、どこにもかしこにも花、花、花。\n→ Then, although it was dreary up to the other day, everywhere were flowers, flowers, flowers.",
 "何処へも": "فِي لَا مَكَان (In no place.)  [nowhere]\nمثال: 私は日曜日にはどこへも行きません。\n→ I am not going anywhere on Sunday.",
 "何処も": "فِي كُلِّ مَكَانٍ (In or to all locations under discussion.)  [everywhere]\nمثال: 春になるとどこも美しく見える。\n→ Everywhere looks beautiful in the spring. / فِي لَا مَكَان (In no place.)  [nowhere (with neg. verb)]\nمثال: 彼らには、ほかにどこも行くところがありません。\n→ They have nowhere else to go.",
 "何処もかも": "جَمِيع أَنْحَاء, كُلّ (Everywhere; covering completely.)  [all over]",
 "何処も彼処も": "جَمِيع أَنْحَاء, كُلّ (Everywhere; covering completely.)  [all over]\nمثال: どこもかしこも人が混んでいるようだ。\n→ Everywhere seems to be crowded.",
 "何処やら": "مَكَان مَا (In an uncertain or unspecified location.)  [somewhere] / [somehow]",
 "何処ら": "أَيْن, فين (In, at or to what place.) / حَيْثُ (The place in, at or to which.) / أَيْن (The place in which something happens.)  [where]",
 "何処を如何": "كَيْف, ازاي (In what manner) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what manner:) / كَيْفَ, ازاي (In what state or condition.) / كَمْ, يَا لَ (Used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings in an)  [how]\nemphatic\nمثال: どこをどう考えたら、俺がロボット工学に明るいなどと思うんだろうか。\n→ Where did you come up with the idea that I'm familiar with robotics and such I wonder?",
 "何分": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some] / أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please] / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]\nمثال: なにぶんこんな辺ぴな村に住んでいるので、めったに客は来ない。\n→ Living as I do in a remote village, I seldom have visitors.",
 "何分にも": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "何十": "عَشَرَة, عَشْرَة (The number occurring after nine and before eleven, represented in Arabic numeral)  [(several) tens]\nمثال: 彼は何十冊も英語の本を持っている。\n→ He has dozens of English books.",
 "何卒": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: 浅学非才の私ではありますが、何とぞ皆様のお力を賜りたく、ここにお願い申し上げる次第です。\n→ I may not have much to offer in the way of learning or ability, but I want to do whatever I can for us all and humbly ask for your favor. / [by all means ; without fail]",
 "何奴": "مَن, مين (What person or people; which person or people; asks for the identity of someone;)  [who]",
 "何年": "كَم وَقْتًا, إِلَى مَتَى (Used literally: for what duration.)  [how long]\nمثال: それを建てるのに何年もかかった。\n→ It took many years to build it. / [what year]",
 "何度となく": "طورا بعد طور (Again and again; repeatedly; every time; always; time and again.)  [time after time]",
 "何度も": "كَثِيرًا, غَالِبًا (Frequently; many times on different occasions.)  [often]\nمثال: 彼は戦場で何度も死をうまく逃れた。\n→ He cheated death many times on the battlefield.",
 "何彼と": "بِطَرِيقَةٍ أَو بِأُخرَى (By any means possible.)  [one way or another]\nمثال: 妻がいないと何かと不自由だ。\n→ I am inconvenienced when my wife is away.",
 "何所": "أَيْن, فين (In, at or to what place.) / حَيْثُ (The place in, at or to which.) / أَيْن (The place in which something happens.)  [where]\nمثال: あなたはどこでテレビを見ますか。\n→ Where do you watch television? / كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much (long, far)]",
 "何所やら": "مَكَان مَا (In an uncertain or unspecified location.)  [somewhere] / [somehow]",
 "何故": "لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]\nمثال: あなたはなぜ働いているの。\n→ How come you're still working?",
 "何故かと言うと": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]",
 "何故なら": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]\nمثال: 聞いて驚くなよ！今日から俺はピアノを始めるんだ。なぜなら私は音楽の先生になりたいからだ！\n→ Brace yourselves! From today I'm learning the piano. Why? Because I want to become a music teacher!",
 "何故ならば": "لِأَنَّ (By or for the cause that; on this account that; for the reason that.) / هكذا, بلا سبب (Used alone to refuse to provide a full answer to a question begun with \"why\", us)  [because]\nمثال: その会合は延期されました。なぜならばジョンが病気だったからです。\n→ The meeting was put off because John was sick.",
 "何故に": "لِمَاذَا ((interrogative) for what reason) / لِمَ ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاش ((interrogative) for what reason) / علاه ((interrogative) for what reason)  [why]",
 "何方": "مَن, مين (What person or people; which person or people; asks for the identity of someone;)  [who]\nمثال: 「どなたですか」「お母さんよ」\n→ \"Who is it?\" \"It's your mother.\"",
 "何方か": "أَحَد (One or some person of unspecified or indefinite identity.)  [someone]\nمثال: 留守中どなたか見えましたか。\n→ Was anybody here while I was out?",
 "何方付かず": "غَيْر حَاسِم, مُتَرَدِّد (Of a person, not decisive, not marked by promptness or decision.)  [indecisive]",
 "何方道": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]\nمثال: どっちみち、関係ないよ。\n→ Either way, it's not important.",
 "何時": "مَتَى (at what time, as a direct question) / إمتى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / امتى (at what time, as a direct question) / فوقتاش (at what time, as a direct question) / حِينَمَا, عِنْدَمَا (During the time that; at the time of the action of the following clause or parti) / مَتَى (At what time; at which time.)  [when]\nusu. as いつ何時 / [what time]",
 "何時か": "يَوْمًا مَا (Sometime; at some unspecified time in the future.)  [someday]\nمثال: いつか君は成功する。\n→ You will succeed some day.",
 "何時かは": "عَاجِلاً أَم آجِلاً, عَاجِلاً أَو آجِلاً (Eventually, at some undetermined time in the not-too-distant future.)  [sooner or later]\nmore emphatic version of 何時か\nمثال: 美しいバラもいつかは萎れる。\n→ The fairest rose is at last withered.",
 "何時から": "كَم وَقْتًا, إِلَى مَتَى (Used literally: for what duration.)  [how long]\nمثال: テレビはいつからあるの？\n→ When did TV appear?",
 "何時ぞや": "مُنْذُ بِضْعَةْ أَيَّام, بِالْأَمْس (Recently; lately; a few days ago.)  [the other day]",
 "何時でも": "دَائِمًا, أَبَدًا (At all times; throughout all time; since the beginning.)  [always]\nمثال: 私はいつでも喜んでお手伝いします。\n→ I am always ready to help you. / مَتَى, مَتَى مَا (At any time that.) / كُلَّمَا (Every time that.)  [whenever (you like)]\nمثال: あなたはいつでも歓迎されています。\n→ You will be welcome at any time.",
 "何時なりと": "مَتَى, مَتَى مَا (At any time that.) / كُلَّمَا (Every time that.)  [whenever]",
 "何時にも増して": "خُصُوصًا, خَاصَّةً (Particularly; to a greater extent than is normal.)  [especially]",
 "何時の日か": "يَوْمًا مَا (Sometime; at some unspecified time in the future.)  [someday]\nمثال: 私はいつの日かアフリカに行きたい。\n→ I want to go to Africa someday.",
 "何時の日にか": "يَوْمًا مَا (Sometime; at some unspecified time in the future.)  [someday]",
 "何時の間に": "مَتَى (at what time, as a direct question) / إمتى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / امتى (at what time, as a direct question) / فوقتاش (at what time, as a direct question) / حِينَمَا, عِنْدَمَا (During the time that; at the time of the action of the following clause or parti) / مَتَى (At what time; at which time.)  [when]",
 "何時までも": "إِلَى الْأَبَد (For all time, for all eternity; for a lifetime; for an infinite amount of time.)  [forever]\nمثال: 私はいつまでも彼の名を覚えている。\n→ I still bear his name in mind.",
 "何時も": "دَائِمًا, أَبَدًا (At all times; throughout all time; since the beginning.)  [always]\nمثال: 彼はいつも学校に遅れる。\n→ He is always late for school. / أَبَدًا (At no time; on no occasion; in no circumstance.)  [never]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: 私は日曜日にはいつも家にいない。\n→ I'm never at home on Sundays. / عَادِيّ (Most commonly occurring; typical.)  [usual]\nمثال: いつものところでいつもの人達に会った。\n→ I met the usual people at the usual place.",
 "何時ものごとく": "كَالْعَادَة, كَالْمُعْتَاد (As is usually the case.)  [as usual]",
 "何時もの通りに": "كَالْعَادَة, كَالْمُعْتَاد (As is usually the case.)  [as usual]\nمثال: 彼はいつもの通り遅れてきた。\n→ He came late as usual.",
 "何時何分": "مَتَى (at what time, as a direct question) / إمتى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / امتى (at what time, as a direct question) / فوقتاش (at what time, as a direct question) / حِينَمَا, عِنْدَمَا (During the time that; at the time of the action of the following clause or parti) / مَتَى (At what time; at which time.)  [when]",
 "何時何時": "مَتَى (at what time, as a direct question) / إمتى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / متى (at what time, as a direct question) / امتى (at what time, as a direct question) / فوقتاش (at what time, as a direct question) / حِينَمَا, عِنْدَمَا (During the time that; at the time of the action of the following clause or parti) / مَتَى (At what time; at which time.)  [when]\nemphatic",
 "何某": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]\nusu. in the form なにがしか / [certain person ; Mr So-and-so] / أَي, إِي (The name of the Latin script letter I/i.)  [I]",
 "何様": "أَحَد (One or some person of unspecified or indefinite identity.)  [a someone]\noften used sarcastically\nمثال: 自分を何様だと思っているのだ、人をそんな風に見て。\n→ Who do you think you are, to look at me like this? / مطلقا, على الإطلاق (In an absolute or unconditional manner; utterly, positively, wholly.)  [absolutely]",
 "何気ない": "غَيْر مُكْتَرِث, لَامُبَالٍ (Indifferent; unconcerned; behaving as if detached.)  [nonchalant]\nمثال: 何気なく言った言葉も誰かを傷つけることがある。\n→ A casual remark can hurt someone. / عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]",
 "何気なく": "عَنْ غَفْلَةٍ (Without meaning to, in an unintentional manner, not intentionally.)  [unintentionally]",
 "何気に": "عَنْ غَيْرِ قَصْدٍ, بِدُونِ قَصْدٍ (Unintentionally; because of an oversight.)  [inadvertently]\nمثال: なにげに話を聞いていたのね。\n→ You were just listening to the talk, without thinking. / بِصِدْقٍ (In a truthful manner)  [truthfully] / [after realizing ; without knowing]",
 "何気無い": "غَيْر مُكْتَرِث, لَامُبَالٍ (Indifferent; unconcerned; behaving as if detached.)  [nonchalant]\nمثال: 何気なく言った言葉も誰かを傷つけることがある。\n→ A casual remark can hurt someone. / عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]",
 "何気無く": "عَنْ غَفْلَةٍ (Without meaning to, in an unintentional manner, not intentionally.)  [unintentionally]",
 "何物": "[what kind of thing]\nمثال: 何ものにもまして私は健康になりたい。\n→ Above all, I want to be healthy. / أَيُّ شَيْءٍ (Any object, act, state, event, or fact whatsoever; a thing of any kind; somethin)  [anything (else)]\nas 〜にも, 〜でもない, etc.\nمثال: 水がなかったならば、何物も生きることはできないだろう。\n→ Were it not for water, nothing could live.",
 "何百": "مِٱئَة, مِئَة (A numerical value equal to 100 (10²), occurring after ninety-nine; ten times ten)  [hundreds]\nمثال: 何百羽とキジを撃った。\n→ We shot pheasants by the hundred.",
