 "作する": "فَعَلَ, صَنَعَ (To create.) / جَعَلَ (To cause to be.) / جَعَلَ (To force to do.) / جَعَلَ (To indicate or suggest to be.)  [to make]",
 "作り": "فَعَلَ, صَنَعَ (To create.) / جَعَلَ (To cause to be.) / جَعَلَ (To force to do.) / جَعَلَ (To indicate or suggest to be.)  [making]\nمثال: あの家はレンガ造りだ。\n→ That house is built of bricks. / ظُهُور (The act of appearing or coming into sight; the act of becoming visible to the ey) / مَظْهَر (A thing seen; a phenomenon; an apparition.) / مَظْهَر, شَكْل (The way something looks; personal presence) / شَكْل (Apparent likeness; the way which something or someone appears to others.)  [appearance (attire, make-up, etc.)] / بَنَى (To form by combining materials or parts.)  [build]\nمثال: 彼女の顔のつくりの中で目が一番いい。\n→ Her eyes are her best feature. / سَاشِيمِي (dish of slices of raw fish or meat)  [sashimi]",
 "作りこむ": "فَعَلَ, صَنَعَ (To create.) / جَعَلَ (To cause to be.) / جَعَلَ (To force to do.) / جَعَلَ (To indicate or suggest to be.)  [to make (with great attention to detail)] / [to build (something) into]",
 "作りつけ": "مَبْنِيّ, مُدْمَج (Constructed as a nondetachable part of a larger structure.) / مُضَمَّن (Being an included feature that normally comes as an extra.)  [built-in]\nمثال: 私の家の壁に本棚が作り付けになっている。\n→ The bookshelves are built into the walls of my room.",
 "作りつける": "صَلَّحَ (to mend or repair) / أَصْلَحَ (to mend or repair)  [to fix (e.g. to a wall)] / نَبَات (An organism that is not an animal, especially an organism capable of photosynthe) / زَرَعَ, غَرَسَ (To place (a seed or plant) in soil or other substrate in order that it may live )  [to plant]",
 "作り上げる": "اِنْتَهَى, أَكْمَلَ (To finish; to make done; to reach the end.) / كَامِل (With all parts included; with nothing missing; full.) / ذَرِيع (Generic intensifier.)  [to complete]\nمثال: 同社は新製品を作り上げた。\n→ The company crafted a new product. / اِفْتَرَى, اِخْتَلَقَ (To invent and form; to forge; to devise falsely.)  [to fabricate]\nمثال: 彼は王についての物語を作り上げた。\n→ He made up a story about the king.",
 "作り事": "فَبْرَكَة (That which is fabricated; a falsehood.)  [fabrication]\nمثال: 彼の話は作りごとだったとわかった。\n→ What he had said proved to be a myth.",
 "作り付け": "مَبْنِيّ, مُدْمَج (Constructed as a nondetachable part of a larger structure.) / مُضَمَّن (Being an included feature that normally comes as an extra.)  [built-in]\nمثال: 私の家の壁に本棚が作り付けになっている。\n→ The bookshelves are built into the walls of my room.",
 "作り付ける": "صَلَّحَ (to mend or repair) / أَصْلَحَ (to mend or repair)  [to fix (e.g. to a wall)] / نَبَات (An organism that is not an animal, especially an organism capable of photosynthe) / زَرَعَ, غَرَسَ (To place (a seed or plant) in soil or other substrate in order that it may live )  [to plant]",
 "作り出す": "صَنَعَ, أَنْتَجَ (To make things, usually on a large scale, with tools and either physical labor o)  [to manufacture]\nمثال: 過ちのない者は何も作り出せない。\n→ He who makes no mistakes makes nothing. / اِخْتَرَعَ (To design a new process or mechanism.)  [to invent]\nمثال: もしも神が存在しないのならば、神を造り出す必要があろう。\n→ If God did not exist, it would be necessary to invent him.",
 "作り名": "اِسْم مُسْتَعَار (A fictitious name (more literally, a false name), as those used by writers and m)  [pseudonym]",
 "作り変える": "حَوَّلَ (To transform or change (something) into another form, substance, state, or produ)  [to convert]\nمثال: 彼女は自分の古い衣服をもっと流行に見えるように作りかえた。\n→ She altered her old clothes to make them look more fashionable.",
 "作り手": "صَانِع, صَائِغ (Someone who makes; a person or thing that makes or produces something.)  [maker] / فَلَّاح, فَلَّاحَة (Someone or something that farms, as:)  [farmer]",
 "作り方": "بِنَاء, تَشْيِيد (The process of constructing.)  [construction]\nمثال: ケイトはケーキの作り方を知っています。\n→ Kate knows how to make a cake. / وَصْفَة (Now especially, a set of instructions for making or preparing food dishes.)  [recipe] / [how to grow (something)]",
 "作り替える": "حَوَّلَ (To transform or change (something) into another form, substance, state, or produ)  [to convert]\nمثال: 彼女は自分の古い衣服をもっと流行に見えるように作りかえた。\n→ She altered her old clothes to make them look more fashionable.",
 "作り物": "تَقْلِيد (The act of imitating.)  [imitation] / خَيَال, رِوَايَة (Literary type using invented or imaginative writing, instead of real facts, usua)  [fiction] / زينة (Any item that adorns, enriches, or beautifies; something added by way of embelli)  [decoration (e.g. for a festival)] / [theatrical prop (esp. a large prop in noh or kyogen, e.g. tree, well, boat)]",
