 "供える": "اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer]\nمثال: お墓には供花が供えられていた。\n→ An offering of flowers had been placed at the grave.",
 "供え物": "قُرْبَان (gerund of offer)  [offering (e.g. to the gods)]",
 "供す": "اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer] / عَبَدَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / خَدَمَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / قَدَّمَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / أَرْسَلَ (To lead off with the first delivery over the net in tennis, volleyball, ping pon) / خَدَمَ (To be in military service.) / إِرْسَال (An act of putting the ball or shuttlecock in play in various games.)  [to serve (food and drink)] / اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer (to the gods)]",
 "供する": "اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer]\nمثال: 小生のレポートをご高覧に供したいと思います。\n→ I would like to submit my report for your perusal. / عَبَدَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / خَدَمَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / قَدَّمَ (To provide a service (or, by extension, a product, especially food or drink).) / أَرْسَلَ (To lead off with the first delivery over the net in tennis, volleyball, ping pon) / خَدَمَ (To be in military service.) / إِرْسَال (An act of putting the ball or shuttlecock in play in various games.)  [to serve (food and drink)]\nمثال: 最初に来た者が最初に食物を供される。\n→ First come, first served. / اِقْتِرَاح (A proposal that has been made.) / اِقْتَرَحَ, قَدَّمَ (To propose or express one's willingness (to do something).) / قَدَّمَ (To present (something) to God or gods, as a gesture of worship or as a sacrifice)  [to offer (to the gods)]",
 "供与": "مِعْطَاء (Having the tendency to give; generous.)  [giving]\nمثال: クレジットとは銀行によって自由に使えることが許されている金額、すなわち信用供与、ローンです。\n→ Credit is the amount or sum placed at a person's disposal by a bank; a loan of money.",
