 "依怙地": "مُتَعَنِّت, عَنِيد (Stubbornly adhering to an opinion, purpose, or course, usually with implied unre)  [obstinate]",
 "依怙贔屓": "تَفْضِيل (The unfair favouring of one person or group at the expense of another.)  [favouritism]\nمثال: あの先生には女子学生をえこひいきする傾向がある。\n→ That teacher tends to be partial to female students.",
 "依拠": "اِسْتِنَاد (The state of being dependent, of relying upon another.) / إِدْمَان (An irresistible physical or psychological need, especially for a chemical substa)  [dependence]\nمثال: 事業を継続しながら、事業が依拠している不動産を切り売りしていくことなど非現実的なのだ。\n→ It's ludicrous to continue business operations while selling off bit by bit the land on which your business depends.",
 "依然": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nمثال: ３人が依然行方不明です。\n→ Three people are still missing.",
 "依然として": "سَاكِن, ثَابِت (Not moving; calm.) / سَاكِنًا (Without motion.) / لَا يَزَال, مَا زَالَ (Up to a time, as in the preceding time.) / رَغِم ذٰلِك, مَعَ ذٰلِك (Nevertheless.)  [still]\nمثال: 依然として彼から便りがない。\n→ I still haven't heard from him.",
 "依頼": "طَلَبَ (to express the need or desire for) / طَلَب, مَسْأَلَة (Act of requesting (with the adposition at in the presence of possessives, and on)  [request]\nمثال: 事務弁護士に遺言状の作成を依頼した。\n→ I asked the solicitor to make out my will. / اِسْتِنَاد (The state of being dependent, of relying upon another.) / إِدْمَان (An irresistible physical or psychological need, especially for a chemical substa)  [dependence]",
