 "倒れる": "وَقَعَ, سَقَطَ (To be moved downwards.) / سَقَطَ (To happen; to come to pass; to chance or light (upon).) / سُقُوط, هُوِيّ (The act of moving to a lower position under the effect of gravity.)  [to fall (over, down)]\nمثال: 彼は横にばったり倒れた。\n→ He fell flat on the floor. / اِنْهَار (To break apart and fall down suddenly; to cave in.) / اِنْهِيَار (The act of collapsing.)  [to collapse]\nمثال: 彼は過労で倒れた。\n→ My father fell ill because he worked too hard. / [to be confined to bed (with an illness) ; to come down with]\nمثال: 彼はいまを盛りにと言う時に倒れた。\n→ He was cut down in his prime. / مَاتَ (to stop living) / تُوُفِّيَ (to stop living) / زَهْر اَلطَّاوِلَة, زَهْر اَلنَّرْد (An isohedral polyhedron, usually a cube, with numbers or symbols on each side an)  [to die]\nocc. written as 斃れる, 仆れる",
