 "傍流": "فَرْع, غُصْن (The woody part of a tree arising from the trunk and usually dividing.)  [branch (of a river)] / فَرْع, غُصْن (The woody part of a tree arising from the trunk and usually dividing.)  [branch]",
 "傍焼き": "حَسَد, غَبْط (A state of being jealous; a jealous attitude.)  [jealousy]",
 "傍聴": "اِسْتِمَاع (An act by which something or somebody is listened to.)  [listening (to a lecture, hearing, parliament session, etc.)]\nمثال: 時々、政治家の一人がテレビの討論会に出て傍聴者の意見を押さえつけようとする場面をみる。\n→ Sometimes, one of the politicians can be seen trying to keep the audience's opinions under control during televised debates.",
 "傍聴人": "متفرج (One who makes observations, monitors or takes notice.)  [observer]\nمثال: 裁判官は傍聴人に静寂にするように命じた。\n→ The judge charged the audience to be silent.",
 "傍聴者": "متفرج (One who makes observations, monitors or takes notice.)  [observer]",
 "傍若無人": "تَكَبُّر, غُرُور (The state of being arrogant; a type of extreme or foolish pride in which someone)  [arrogance]\nمثال: 傍若無人の振る舞いだね。\n→ They are cutting loose.",
 "傍観者": "مُتَفَرِّج (A person who, although present at some event, does not take part in it; an obser)  [bystander]\nمثال: 傍観者にはゲームの大部分がみえる。\n→ Onlookers see most of the game.",
 "傍訓": "مُلَاحَظَة هَامِشِيَّة (A note in the margin of a document.)  [marginal notes]",
 "傍註": "مُلَاحَظَة هَامِشِيَّة (A note in the margin of a document.)  [marginal notes]",
 "傍輩": "رَفِيق, رَفِيقَة (A mate, companion, or associate.) / رَفِيق, رَفِيقَة (A fellow socialist, communist or other similarly politically aligned person.) / رَفِيق, رَفِيقَة (A non-hierarchical title, functionally similar to \"Mr.\", \"Mrs.\", \"Miss\", \"Ms.\" e)  [comrade]",
 "傍題": "عَنَاوِين فَرْعِيَّة, عُنْوَان فَرْعِيّ (A heading below or after a title.) / تَرْجَمَة, سَتْرَجَة (Textual versions of the dialogue in films (and similar media such as television ) / تَرْجَمَ (To create subtitles for the dialogue in a film.)  [subtitle (e.g. of a book)]",
 "傑": "قِمَّة (The highest or uppermost part of something.)  [the top (e.g. top ten)]",
 "傑作": "تُحْفَة, رَائِعَة (A piece of work that has been given much critical praise, especially one that is)  [masterpiece]\nمثال: その偉大な画家の傑作が壁にさかさまにかかっているを見て、彼は驚いた。\n→ He was surprised to find the great artist's masterpiece hung on the wall upside down. / مَرِح, مُضْحِك (Very funny; causing great merriment and laughter.)  [(unintentionally) hilarious]\nمثال: わははは！そりゃ傑作だ！\n→ A-ha-ha-ha! What a blunder!",
 "傑士": "بَطَل, بَطَلَة (To act as a hero (brave person; role model; or protagonist).)  [hero]",
 "傑物": "عِمْلَاق (A mythical human or humanoid of very great size.)  [giant]\nمثال: さすがは、王子様ですわね。きっとただならない傑物の素質をお持ちなのですわ。\n→ Isn't that just what you'd expect from the prince? He certainly has the character of a truly great man.",
 "傘": "مِظَلَّة, شَمْسِيَّة (A cloth-covered frame used for protection against rain or sun.) / وَاقٍ, الْوَاقِي (Anything that provides similar protection.)  [umbrella]\nمثال: タクシーに傘を忘れてしまった。\n→ I left my umbrella in the cab. / ظِلّ, مَظَلَّة (Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.)  [shade (of a lamp)]",
 "備え": "تَحْضِير, إِعْدَاد (The act of preparing or getting ready.)  [preparation]\nمثال: このお金は、もしものときの備えです。\n→ This money is for a rainy day. / دِفَاع, حِمَايَة (The action of defending or protecting from attack, danger, or injury.) / دِفاع (Anything employed to oppose attack(s).) / دِفاع (Government policy or (infra)structure related to the military.)  [defenses] / نَشْر (The distribution of military forces, especially prior to battle.)  [deployment]",
 "備えつける": "زَوَّدَ (To furnish (with), cause to be present, supply.)  [to provide]\nمثال: その船はレーダーを備え付けていない。\n→ The ship is not equipped with radar.",
 "備える": "زَوَّدَ (To furnish (with), cause to be present, supply.)  [to provide]\nمثال: このビルは非常階段を備えている。\n→ The building is equipped with emergency stairs. / [to prepare for ; to make preparations for]\nمثال: 不時にそなえなくてはいけない。\n→ You should be prepared for emergencies. / مَلَكَ, اِمْتَلَكَ (To have (something) as, or as if as, an owner; to have, to own.)  [to possess (all that is needed)]\nمثال: 食虫植物は、昆虫を捕らえるための様々な種類の罠を備えている。\n→ Insect-eating plants are equipped with various kinds of traps to catch insects. / [to be born with ; to have since birth]",
 "備え付け": "مُعَدَّات, تَجْهِيزَات (Any items used in equipping something or someone, for example things needed for )  [equipment]",
 "備え付ける": "زَوَّدَ (To furnish (with), cause to be present, supply.)  [to provide]\nمثال: その船はレーダーを備え付けていない。\n→ The ship is not equipped with radar.",
 "備に": "بِالتَّفْصِيل, تَفْصِيلًا (Thoroughly; including every detail; with all particulars.)  [in detail]",
 "備付": "مُعَدَّات, تَجْهِيزَات (Any items used in equipping something or someone, for example things needed for )  [equipment]",
 "備品": "مُعَدَّات, تَجْهِيزَات (Any items used in equipping something or someone, for example things needed for )  [equipment]\nمثال: 研究所用備品は３月１５日までに間違いなく配達できます。\n→ I'm certain we can deliver the laboratory equipment by March 15th.",
 "備忘録": "دَفْتَر, مُذَكِّرَة (A book (physical or digital) in which notes or memoranda are written.) / كَمْبْيُوتَر مَحْمُول, حَاسُوب مَحْمُول (Ellipsis of notebook computer (“laptop computer”).)  [notebook]",
