 "傷": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [wound]\nمثال: 海水が傷にしみて痛いよ。\n→ The seawater stings my cut. / صَدْع (A thin and usually jagged space opened in a previously solid material.)  [crack]\nمثال: 彼の額の傷は目立つ。\n→ The scar on his forehead is conspicuous. / عَيْبٌ (defect, fault)  [flaw]\nمثال: ここに傷があるので安くしてください。\n→ There's a scratch here. Could you give me a discount? / بُقْعَة (A discolored spot or area caused by spillage or other contact with certain fluid)  [stain (on one's reputation)]\nمثال: クリスはとてもむなしく思い、立ち直れないほどに、心に大きな傷を受けました。\n→ Chris' heart felt so empty and damaged that it couldn't be repaired.",
 "傷つきやすい": "هَشّ (Readily disrupted or destroyed.)  [fragile]",
 "傷つき安い": "هَشّ (Readily disrupted or destroyed.)  [fragile]",
 "傷つける": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [to wound]\nمثال: 他人を傷つけることはよくない。\n→ It is bad to hurt others. / [to hurt someone's feelings (pride, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼の感情を傷つけるのを恐れて、本当の事を言わなかった。\n→ Afraid of hurting his feelings, I didn't tell him the truth. / عُطْل, ضَرَر (Injury or harm; the condition or measure of something not being intact.)  [to damage]",
 "傷み": "أَلَمٌ (The condition or fact of suffering or anguish especially mental, as opposed to p) / آلَمَ, يُؤْلِمُ (To hurt; to put to bodily uneasiness or anguish; to afflict with uneasy sensatio) / آلَمَ, يُؤْلِمُ (To render uneasy in mind; to disquiet; to distress; to grieve.)  [pain]\nesp. 痛み\nمثال: ここにしつこい痛みがあります。\n→ I have a persistent pain here. / عُطْل, ضَرَر (Injury or harm; the condition or measure of something not being intact.)  [damage]\nesp. 傷み\nمثال: モモの皮は傷みやすい。\n→ The skin of peaches bruises easily.",
 "傷む": "جَرَحَ (To cause (a person or animal) physical pain and/or injury.) / أَلِمَ, وَجِعَ (To be painful.)  [to hurt]\nesp. 痛む\nمثال: 彼はいま歯が痛むのでよくかむことができない。\n→ He can't chew well, because he has a toothache now. / [to be injured ; to be spoiled (e.g. food)]\nesp. 傷む\nمثال: 傷むのを防ぐために、遠海で捕獲した魚は直ちに冷却される。\n→ To avoid spoiling, fish caught far out at sea are immediately cooled or even frozen.",
 "傷める": "جَرَحَ (To cause (a person or animal) physical pain and/or injury.) / أَلِمَ, وَجِعَ (To be painful.)  [to hurt]\nusu. 痛める\nمثال: 彼は氷の上で転んで脚を傷めた。\n→ He fell down on the ice and hurt his leg. / ضَرَرٌ (Physical injury; hurt; damage.) / ضَرَّ أَضَرَّ (To damage, hurt, or injure something, usually an inanimate object.)  [to harm]\nusu. 傷める / قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [to worry]\nusu. 痛める / [to cause financial loss ; to hurt one's pocket]\nusu. 痛める",
 "傷バン": "ضِمَادَة, لاصِق طِبِّي (An adhesive bandage, a small piece of fabric or plastic that may be stuck to the)  [band-aid]",
 "傷付きやすい": "هَشّ (Readily disrupted or destroyed.)  [fragile]",
 "傷付き安い": "هَشّ (Readily disrupted or destroyed.)  [fragile]",
 "傷付ける": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [to wound]\nمثال: 他人を傷つけることはよくない。\n→ It is bad to hurt others. / [to hurt someone's feelings (pride, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼の感情を傷つけるのを恐れて、本当の事を言わなかった。\n→ Afraid of hurting his feelings, I didn't tell him the truth. / عُطْل, ضَرَر (Injury or harm; the condition or measure of something not being intact.)  [to damage]",
 "傷創": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [wound]",
 "傷口": "جُرْح, جِرَاحَة (An injury, such as a cut, stab, or tear, to a (usually external) part of the bod) / جَرَحَ (To hurt or injure (someone) by cutting, piercing, or tearing the skin.)  [(opening of a) wound]\nمثال: 母は傷口にばんそうこうをつけてくれた。\n→ Mom applied the plaster to the cut.",
